# HatchGrab — Cursor working rules

This file is NOT a manual. It holds only rules about how to work in this repo that are
not in the manual. Everything else lives in one place, on purpose.

---

## 1. The manual is the single source of truth

**`docs/reference-manual.md` (V9.1, July 2026) is the single source of truth** for
architecture, schema, invariants, conventions, feature behaviour, and the backlog.

- **Read it at the start of any non-trivial task.** Not skimmed after the fact — read
  before designing or editing. It is long; read the sections your task touches, plus the
  changelog entries since the last version you saw.
- **Where code and the manual disagree, the manual wins.** Change the code, not the rule.
- **Unless the manual is demonstrably stale** — in which case **flag it and stop**;
  do not silently follow the code. Say which section is stale, what the code actually
  does, and what the evidence is. The manual is corrected by decision, never by drift.
- **Do not copy manual content into this file.** Not a section, not a summary, not a
  "quick reference". A précis is just a smaller duplicate, and it drifts. Link to the
  section instead.

*This file previously held a verbatim copy of the manual at V4 (May 2026) — 842 lines,
five versions and ~14 months of decisions out of date. It primed every Cursor session
with a codebase that no longer existed (e.g. V4 described `keep_screen_on` as a
truck-level DB column; V9.0 retired it to per-device localStorage). That copy was
deleted on 26 July 2026. It is recoverable in full from git: `git show HEAD:.cursor/rules`.
Two-hand-maintained-records drift is a failure class the manual names as recurring — do
not restart it here.*

---

## Android build protocol (2026-07)

*Added 26 July 2026. NOTE: no Android protocol section existed in this file before this — the rules below were dictated, not amended in place. Item 3 is numbered to match the protocol as dictated; the earlier items were never written down here, so nothing above item 3 is recorded.*

**3. Reporting — SUPERSEDED.** Do NOT return the full summary to chat. The full report goes to `docs/android-report.md`, overwritten each task. Only a **two-line summary** goes to chat.

**3a. Partial reports are REQUIRED.** If a task is interrupted, blocked, or left partial, STILL write `docs/android-report.md` with what was established, what remains, and what blocked you. A partial report is required, not optional — an unwritten report loses the work if the session ends.

**File roles — these three are never to be confused:**

| File | Role | Rule |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `docs/android.md` | Durable append-only working log: facts, work list, decisions, corrections. | **NEVER overwrite.** Append only. |
| `docs/android-report.md` | Transient per-task report. | Overwritten every task. |
| `docs/last-report.md` | Belongs to a **separate parallel workstream**. | **NEVER read, write, or overwrite it.** |
